  // own rule -- bug fixes, no new API surface.] // [0.39.203: COS test environments with a real VM backend -- James: 'this? if not expand cos to fully fit idearium's and nexus' needs' (uploaded cos-standalone-windows-vm.zip). The upload is an older standalone extract of the same COS: its qemu-runtime.js is byte-identical to Nexus's, still with no guest command channel and no file sharing, and it lacks Nexus's newer cos/ci and advance-work-phase (it also carried a stray cli/powershell.exe, not imported). So COS itself was expanded. qemu-runtime: opt-in vmConfig.guestAgent (virtio-serial org.qemu.guest_agent.0 on a unix socket, tcp on Windows) and vmConfig.shareDir (9p -virtfs mount_tag cos_share on a Linux host, a vvfat drive elsewhere); buildQemuArgs returns qga and share endpoints; both default off so every existing VM compartment boots exactly as before (asserted); QEMU_BIN/QEMU_IMG_BIN exported. NEW cos/compartment/guest-agent.js: qemu-guest-agent client -- guest-sync (discards stale channel bytes and the 0xFF sentinel), guest-ping, guest-exec with captured output, guest-exec-status polling with base64 out/err decoding, agent errors thrown with the agent's own description, per-command timeout; connectWhenReady retries until the guest boots. NEW cos/testenv/index.js: one API, two backends, one result shape -- process (SandboxRunner, clean env, watchdog) and vm (ephemeral qcow2 overlay of a read-only base image, network none, the branch shared in over 9p and mounted at /mnt/cos, each target run in the guest via guest-exec, guest-shutdown + kill, overlay discarded so nothing persists); auto picks vm only when capabilities() finds qemu-system-x86_64 and qemu-img on PATH, a base image (COS_TESTENV_BASE_IMAGE) that exists, and a Linux host -- otherwise process, and the result always says which ran and why; vm requested but unavailable is refused with the reason, never silently downgraded. lib/repo-run.js now runs through cos/testenv (testBackend auto|process|vm) and r