    // (docs/2026-09-13-massive-codebase-orchestration-phasemap.spec) is
    // referenced by the newer doc but missing from this export.] // [0.39.126: cortex/tools/table-materializer.js + CLI + node-export occurrence tracking; components table migrated (194 created, 71 filed as gaps, 29 bumped)] //   // [0.39.125: cli/decompose.js generalized to work on any real monolith, not just cortex/boot.js -- James: "I want to be able to use it in case any monoliths happen. Which it has in ollama and copilot." Checked all 3 real monoliths directly, not guessed: cortex/boot.js uses `p === '/x'` (the only convention the tool matched before); copilot/server.js ALSO uses `p`, but in both orders -- 8 blocks path-first, 18 method-first (`method === 'GET' && p === '/x'`), which the old path-first-only header regex silently missed; guardian/server.js uses a different path variable entirely (`url.pathname`), overwhelmingly method-first -- matched ZERO blocks before this pass (confirmed via a real `analyze` run: 0 of 4174 lines). ollama/server.js checked too: already decomposed to 118 lines with its own routes/ dir, genuinely nothing left to extract there right now. findRouteBlocks now captures the route condition VERBATIM (condText) instead of reconstructing it from parsed parts -- extract() reuses it unmodified on write-back, so a rewritten guardian route still reads url.pathname, never introduces an undefined `p`. Found and fixed a real, pre-existing bug in the walker along the way, exposed by guardian's actual /version handler (line 1678): `content.match(/version['\":\\s]+['\"v]?(\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+)/i)` -- a regex literal with a bare quote inside a character class, which the old walker (no regex-literal awareness) misread as a string delimiter, silently absorbing real braces until a stray same-type quote resolved it lines later. Before the fix this measured /version's block at 2504 lines (1672-4175, past EOF), swallowing every real route after it -- guardian only reported 5 blocks instead of the real 49. Built a shared, regex-aware walkBraceBlock() (handles character classes, where an unescaped `/` does not end the regex, using the standard regex-vs-division heuristic every real JS tokenizer uses) and replaced both findRouteBlocks' and findRegistryBlocks' previously-duplicated inline walkers with it -- one real fix instead of two copies to keep in sync. Verified against all 3 real targets: cortex/boot.js 57->59 (found 2 real method-first /api/personas routes the old regex missed, confirmed by direct source read, not a false positive), copilot/server.js 8->19, guardian/server.js 0->49 (all within the real handleExtendedRoutes 1544-3392 range). Dynamic routes (.startsWith/.test regex routes, 6 real ones in guardian) deliberately still excluded -- a genuinely different extraction shape, out of scope for this pass, not silently mismatched. New tests/modules/test-decompose.js (6/6: p-convention regression, url.pathname generalization, method-first-order generalization, the exact regex-brace-bug reproduction as a GATE test, dynamic-route exclusion, and extract's verbatim condText preservation), registered in run-all.js. No extraction run against guardian/copilot yet -- this pass only fixes and verifies the analyze-mode tool itself; extraction stays one route at a time per the tool's own stated scope, pending direction on which routes to move first.] // [0.39.124: real .injection node type -- James: "every time something gets prepended to a dispatch, there'd be a real node recording what and why," the natural follow-up to v0.39.122's "mountain" fix. Checked first, not built blind: .input already existed (REAL, wired, sovereign copies in guardian/copilot) from an earlier session -- only .injection was genuinely missing, confirmed via NODE-TAXONOMY.md (35 slots, no injection entry) and a KNOWN_TYPES grep. Grounded in exactly one real construction site: copilot/tool-runtime.js's makeNcpCallModel inner callModel -- the exact function v0.39.122 patched. makeOllamaCallModel checked and excluded: ollama-bridge's /api/chat takes a native `tools` param, never text-injects a guide, so there is no second real site to fold in. New lib/node-schemas/schema.injection (status:REAL, 8 fields -- provider/primed/injectedSystemPrompt/injectedToolGuide/toolCount/promptLength/idleMsThreshold/msSinceLastPrimed -- every one traced to a real variable already in scope at that call site, nothing invented) + copilot/schemas/schema.injection (sovereign copy, since copilot owns the construction site) + 'injection' added to KNOWN_TYPES (36 total). Real writer wired directly into makeNcpCallModel's callModel: writes a real .injection node to copilot/data/nodes/injection/ every call, primed or full-context, non-fatal on write failure -- same discipline this file's own gapField.report() calls already use. INJECTION_NODES_DIR made overridable via COPILOT_INJECTION_DIR env var for test isolation, matching test-node-index.js's own JAA_DATA_DIR redirect convention. New tests/modules/test-injection-node-type.js (4/4: schema registration, a full-context call writes a schema-valid node, a same-provider repeat call within PROVIDER_IDLE_MS writes primed:true with real msSinceLastPrimed evidence and a measurably smaller promptLength, a genuinely different provider is not treated as already primed). tests/modules/test-copilot-tool-runtime.js re-run unaffected: 12/12.] // [0.39.123: real mock_data_finder .tool. James: "can you create a .tool to find mock data also." Real, distinct from stub_finder (0.39.121) -- that tool finds CODE SHAPES (a stub function, a mock-named identifier); this one finds literal DATA VALUES that read as real content but are conventional fakes, regardless of what the surrounding code or variable is named: placeholder emails (example.com/test.com/foo.com -- the real, reserved RFC 2606 domains, not a guess), placeholder names ("John Doe"/"Jane Doe"/"Foo Bar"), literal lorem-ipsum text, and placeholder phone numbers (the 555-01xx exchange -- the North American Numbering Plan's own real reserved fictional